ds4-agent
Run the native terminal coding agent with live tools, session save/restore, and a responsive prompt while the model works.

Usage: ds4-agent [options]

Model And Runtime
  -m, --model FILE               GGUF model path. Default: ds4flash.gguf
  --vision FILE                  Vision encoder GGUF for the selected model.
  --metal | --cuda | --cpu       Select the backend explicitly.
  --backend NAME                 Backend name: metal, cuda, or cpu.
  --gpu-vram N[,N,...]|auto      CUDA VRAM budgets per device, in GiB, or auto-detect free VRAM.
  --gpu-devices N[,N,...]        CUDA device indices used by multi-GPU placement.
  --cuda-tensor-parallel         Enable the paired DeepSeek tensor/expert path on an even multi-GPU CUDA placement.
  -c, --ctx N                    Allocated context tokens.
  -t, --threads N                CPU helper threads for host-side/reference work.
  --power N                      GPU duty-cycle target, 1..100. Default: 100
  --ssd-streaming                Metal/CUDA/ROCm: opt in to SSD-backed model streaming instead of full residency.
  --ssd-streaming-cold           SSD streaming: skip default popularity-based expert-cache preload.
  --ssd-streaming-cache-experts N|NGB
      SSD streaming cache target. N requests dynamic expert slots; NGB also reserves two full prefill layers. Either may be reduced to fit the model, graph, context, and backend working set.
  --ssd-streaming-full-layers N  GLM Metal streaming: keep the first N routed layers fully resident. Default: auto from NGB expert budget; use 0 to disable.
  --ssd-streaming-preload-experts N
      SSD streaming: upfront popularity preload count. DeepSeek auto-seeds by default; GLM demand-fills unless N is explicit.
  --simulate-used-memory NGB     Diagnostic: lock N GiB before model load to simulate a smaller-memory machine.
  --prefill-chunk N              Graph prefill chunk size. Default: CUDA TP 2048; PRO long prompts 8192; others 4096.

Agent Options
  -p, --prompt TEXT              Submit an initial prompt after startup.
  --prompt-file FILE             Read the initial prompt from FILE.
  --prefix-file FILE             Preload complete alternating USER:/ASSISTANT: turns before the live task.
  --non-interactive              Run without TUI. With an initial prompt: one turn; otherwise: repeated stdin prompts.
  --raw-prompt                   Non-interactive initial prompt only: omit agent chat/tool text.
  --edit-upto                    Enable anchored [upto] edits and automatic marker insertion.
  -sys, --system TEXT            Extra system prompt. Empty disables extra text.
  --trace FILE                   Write prompt, token, and DSML debug trace.
  --live-context-file FILE       Experiment: mirror text chat into FILE; import edits after tools finish.
  --chdir DIR                    Change working directory before loading runtime assets.

Agent Runtime Commands
  /save                          Save the current session in ~/.ds4/kvcache.
  /compact                       Compact the current session context now.
  /list                          List saved sessions, sorted by recent update time.
  /switch ID                     Load a saved session and show recent history.
  /del ID                        Delete a saved session.
  /strip ID                      Remove KV payload; the text history can be rebuilt later.
  /history [N]                   Show N recent user turns from the current session.
  /hints on|off                  Enable or disable brief programming hints. New and resumed sessions start off.
  /think [N]                     V4.1: set effort 0..100 (default 75) after this turn; rebuilds the prefix.
  /power N                       Set GPU duty cycle percentage, 1..100.
  /new                           Start a fresh session from the system prompt.
  /quit, /exit                   Exit.

More Info
    Runtime full info:         --help runtime
    Sampling full info:        --help sampling
    Distributed inference:     --help distributed
    Steering full info:        --help steering
    Agent sessions:            --help sessions
    Agent commands:            --help commands
    Agent tool system:         --help tools

Examples
  interactive                    ./ds4-agent
  one shot                       ./ds4-agent --non-interactive -p "Create /tmp/hello.c"

